&lt;h1&gt;Senior Account Executive – Medical Communications&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Women&#39;s Health | Medical Education&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; London / Manchester / Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About ApotheCom&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At ApotheCom, an Inizio Medical company, we partner with leading pharmaceutical and biotechnology organisations to create meaningful medical communications that advance scientific understanding and improve patient care. Our teams combine scientific expertise, and creativity to deliver impactful medical education programmes that engage healthcare professionals around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Account Executive&lt;/strong&gt; to join our team, supporting an exciting global &lt;strong&gt;Women&#39;s Health&lt;/strong&gt; account.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a fantastic opportunity to work across a diverse portfolio of medical education programs, collaborating with global clients and experienced diverse teams to deliver high-quality scientific communications. You&#39;ll be part of a busy, supportive account where you&#39;ll develop your client and project management, while contributing to programmes that make an impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate multiple projects from initiation through to delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support a variety of deliverables, including steering committee meetings, expert panels, slide presentations, scientific workshops, educational and training materials, digital education programmes, webinars and videos&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with clients, being a reliable and responsive point of contact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain project timelines, trackers and meeting schedules to ensure projects are delivered on time and within budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with scientific, editorial, creative and digital colleagues to deliver high-quality programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support project financial management, including budget tracking, invoicing and forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify risks and helping implement practical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute ideas that enhance project delivery, team collaboration and client satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be an organised client services professional who enjoys working in a collaborative environment and delivering exceptional client experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience within a medical communications agency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent project management and organisational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and relationship-building skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting project budgets, invoicing and financial tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence working with a variety of teams in a busy environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join ApotheCom?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on an exciting global Women&#39;s Health account delivering innovative medical education programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join a collaborative and highly experienced team that values learning and development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain exposure to several strategic medical education projects and global clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy genuine opportunities for career progression within ApotheCom and the wider Inizio Medical network.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Benefit from flexible hybrid and remote working options, alongside a competitive salary and comprehensive benefits package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re a Senior Account Executive looking to further your career in medical communications we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a great compensation and benefits package including private medical insurance and a company pension, we are happy to talk dynamic working. We are also known for our friendly and informal working environment with Friday socials across our offices, regular wellbeing weeks, and Town Hall events. We offer excellent opportunities for career and personal development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to promoting a culture of diversity, inclusion and belonging. We believe that strength in diversity and inclusivity is a driver of our success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t meet every job requirement? That&#39;s okay! Our company is dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive, and authentic workplace. If you&#39;re excited about this role, but your experience doesn&#39;t perfectly fit every qualification, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right person for this role or others.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://i.imgur.com/UuLTAa2.png&quot; alt=&quot;disability confident committed&quot; width=&quot;311&quot; style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About ApotheCom&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ApotheCom is an exciting leader in the field of medical communications. Drawn together from several backgrounds including the pharmaceutical industry, research, marketing, medical and regulatory writing, sales, publishing, digital media and design, we have the experience and all-round ability to conceive and deliver the best quality medical communications programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Medical Director is a scientific and strategic lead responsible for the quality, accuracy and strategic direction of assigned medical communications workstreams and accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will be accountable for ensuring that scientific content is clinically accurate, strategically aligned, insight-driven and relevant to client medical strategy and agency objectives. You will partner closely with client services, editorial, creative, digital, medical writing and senior scientific leadership to ensure that deliverables meet client expectations, reflect current scientific evidence and support broader communication goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Medical Director serves as a key scientific contact for clients, faculty and external experts, bringing subject matter expertise, sound judgment and a proactive consultative approach to assigned projects. You will lead and contribute to content development plans, elevate the scientific and strategic quality of deliverables, support new business activity and help guide junior scientific team members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To be considered for this role, candidates should have successfully demonstrated Senior Medical Writer-level capabilities and typically bring at least 5 years of experience in medical communications, publications, medical education or a related scientific communications environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Medical Director will report to a Medical Director, Senior Medical Director or senior Scientific Services leader.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic thinking and scientific insight&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accountable for the scientific strategy and quality of assigned accounts, workstreams and deliverables, ensuring alignment with client medical strategy and agency objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads and contributes to content development plans, ensuring deliverables are grounded in evidence and aligned with strategic imperatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interprets and synthesizes complex clinical data, including clinical trial results, congress updates, treatment guidelines, publications and competitive information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translates complex scientific and clinical information into clear, compelling and strategically relevant medical communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides proactive scientific input into publication plans, medical education programs, communication platforms and other client deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifies key scientific insights, evidence gaps and communication opportunities that can strengthen client strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participates in new business pitches, proposals and client onboarding by providing scientific insight and therapeutic area expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client partnership and excellence in delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serves as a key scientific contact for clients, faculty, authors, investigators and external experts, building relationships based on scientific credibility, responsiveness and delivery excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partners with pharmaceutical and biotechnology clients to understand goals, communication objectives, scientific priorities and success measures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviews and elevates scientific content to ensure not only accuracy, but also strategic alignment with client objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures assigned medical communications are clinically relevant, current and reflective of recent advances in the therapeutic area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaises with clients and external experts to support streamlined, efficient development of high-quality deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports the planning and execution of advisory boards, investigator meetings, faculty meetings, congress activities and scientific workshops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipates client needs, flags risks early and recommends solutions to protect scientific quality, timelines and budget expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Teamwork, collaboration and leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partners with Client Services and cross-functional colleagues across creative, digital, editorial, account and specialized services to ensure deliverables meet client expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides day-to-day scientific direction to medical writers, freelancers and junior scientific team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Offers formal and informal mentorship, coaching and performance feedback to junior team members, supporting their scientific growth and delivery quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrates increasing autonomy in account decision-making while knowing when to escalate scientific, client, budget or delivery risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively drives team growth and efficiency, including suggestions for process improvement within the team, cluster or squad.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributes to key strategic priorities, including recruitment, resourcing, business development and operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborates with project and account teams to ensure timelines are realistic, scope is understood and scientific requirements are appropriately planned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Content development and quality oversight&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads or oversees development of scientific content across manuscripts, abstracts, posters, slide decks, advisory board materials, white papers, monographs, congress materials and medical education content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviews and refines medical writing to ensure scientific accuracy, strategic relevance, logical flow, appropriate tone and audience fit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conducts targeted literature reviews and evidence assessments to ensure content reflects current clinical practice and therapeutic developments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintains awareness of good publication practices and appropriate standards for publications, medical education and professional communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides quality control for scientific content developed by internal writers, freelancers and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures reference support, data interpretation, claims and scientific messaging are accurate, balanced and appropriately substantiated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial and operational awareness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understands the financial side of assigned accounts and works with team members to help projects remain in scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides senior scientific input into scopes of work, budgets, timelines and resource planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifies potential changes in project focus, scientific complexity or scope and escalates appropriately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports efficient delivery by balancing scientific excellence with timeline, budget and client-service expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an experienced medical communications professional with strong scientific judgment, strategic curiosity and the confidence to advise clients and guide internal teams. You can move fluidly between detailed content review and broader strategic discussion, and you are comfortable taking ownership of complex scientific deliverables.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience and capabilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree in life sciences, medicine, pharmacy, pharmacology or a related scientific discipline; doctorate-level training preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Typically 5+ years of experience in medical communications, publications, medical education, scientific strategy or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to operate at or above Senior Medical Writer level, including strong content development, data interpretation and client-facing skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of clinical data interpretation, publication development, medical education and pharmaceutical communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead scientific content development with limited oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong client communication skills, including the ability to interact professionally and confidently with clients, faculty and external experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring, guiding or line-managing medical writers, freelancers or junior scientific team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational, financial and administrative discipline, including the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail and strong commitment to scientific accuracy, quality and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Microsoft Word, PowerPoint and Excel; familiarity with literature databases and reference management tools preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel as needed, including occasional weekends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ApotheCom can offer an attractive rewards package, excellent training and development opportunities, a supportive and friendly environment and the opportunity to achieve your potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Pledge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At ApotheCom,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;we value inclusivity, recognize the power of diversity and inspire the next generation of change-makers. We are an equal opportunities employer. We believe in creating a dynamic work environment that values diversity, equity and inclusion. We aim to recruit from a diverse slate of candidates and foster an environment that provides the right conditions for long-term success. We welcome all applications regardless of race, color, religion or belief, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, marital status, military veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation and physical or mental disability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ApotheCom is part of Inizio Medical. Inizio is a strategic partner for health and life sciences with a full suite of medical, marketing, advisory and engagement services.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t meet every job requirement? That&#39;s okay! Our company is dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive, and authentic workplace. If you&#39;re excited about this role, but your experience doesn&#39;t perfectly fit every qualification, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right person for this role or others.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://i.imgur.com/UuLTAa2.png&quot; alt=&quot;disability confident committed&quot; width=&quot;311&quot; style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Account Manager/Senior Account Manager – Medical Communications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;London/Manchester/Hybrid/Remote(UK)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At &lt;strong&gt;Inizio Medical&lt;/strong&gt;, the combined expertise of &lt;strong&gt;ApotheCom, Nucleus Global, and Ashfield Medcomms&lt;/strong&gt;, supported by the specialist skills of &lt;strong&gt;MEDiSTRAVA&lt;/strong&gt;, brings together world-leading medical communications excellence. We create compelling scientific content, connect expert communities, and deliver outcomes that truly matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to continued growth, we&#39;re looking for an Account Manager/Senior Account Manager&amp;nbsp;to join the &lt;strong&gt;ApotheCom&lt;/strong&gt; team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a dynamic and varied role offering the chance to work across a diverse range of projects within a supportive, established, and collaborative team. You&#39;ll grow your expertise and grow your career in an environment that values innovation, quality, and teamwork.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be responsible for leading the delivery of complex scientific communications and Medical Affairs programmes, ensuring projects are executed on time, within budget, and to the highest quality standards. You&#39;ll be a trusted partner to clients, managing risks, financial performance, and cross-functional teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage publications and medical affairs projects from initiation through to completion, including &lt;strong&gt;abstracts, posters, manuscripts, congress deliverables, advisory boards, slide decks, medical education materials, training programmes, scientific platforms&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multiple concurrent projects and workstreams across client programmes, ensuring timely delivery and effective resource management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain project plans, timelines, and status trackers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate multidisciplinary internal teams and external stakeholders to ensure seamless project execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own project financial management, including budget development, forecasting, invoicing, revenue recognition, and profitability tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing Statements of Work (SOWs), monitoring scope, identifying change requests and out-of-scope activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain client relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within a &lt;strong&gt;Medical Communications agency&lt;/strong&gt; in a project/account or programme management role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing &lt;strong&gt;scientific publications&lt;/strong&gt; (including abstracts, posters, and manuscripts) and a broad range of &lt;strong&gt;Medical Affairs deliverables&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to manage multiple complex projects simultaneously while balancing quality, timelines, budgets, and client expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project financial management experience, including budgeting, forecasting, invoicing, and financial reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organisational, planning, and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building client relationships and leading project communications with both internal and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Inizio Medical, we believe our people are our strength. You&#39;ll enjoy:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;competitive salary and benefits package&lt;/strong&gt;, including &lt;strong&gt;private medical insurance&lt;/strong&gt; and a &lt;strong&gt;company pension&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible, hybrid working&lt;/strong&gt; options to support work-life balance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;friendly and inclusive culture&lt;/strong&gt; with regular &lt;strong&gt;Friday socials&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;wellbeing initiatives&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Town Hall events&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional &lt;strong&gt;career development opportunities&lt;/strong&gt; and access to world-class learning resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to promote a culture of &lt;strong&gt;diversity, inclusion, and belonging&lt;/strong&gt;. We believe our differences make us stronger — and that diversity drives innovation, creativity, and success.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t meet every job requirement? That&#39;s okay! Our company is dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive, and authentic workplace. If you&#39;re excited about this role, but your experience doesn&#39;t perfectly fit every qualification, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right person for this role or others.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
